  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 5.2. Increased capacity of member States to strengthen skills and lifelong learning policies, governance models and financing system</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">In May 2021, the task force for the application of the ILO&apos;s &quot;Skills for Trade and Economic Diversification&quot; (STED) methodology completed the study report in the Dairy sector with concrete recommendations endorsed by stakeholders, and the implementation plan was approved in July 2021. The Ministry of Economic Planning, Development and Public Sector Reforms have endorsed the selected implementing partners to carry out training in the dairy sector.

In March 2020, the Malawi STED Guide was endorsed by stakeholders including the Ministries of Labour, Agriculture, Trade, Industry, Economic Planning and department of National Statistics. The government and stakeholders are using the guide to assess skills needs in various sectors and develop new training strategies for them, implemented in the districts Blantyre, Thyolo, Phalombe, Chiradzulu, Mzuzu and Nkhatabay, with 500 people reached through informal training using tailor made training manuals developed by individual TVET Institutions and private sector enterprises for aggregator farmers, reaching 150 youths through the formal Work Integrated Learning (WIL). The ILO convened high-level stakeholder meetings to discuss the drafting of the STED guide,  the Dairy Sector study report and the new training strategy. The discussions and ILO inputs were incorporated into the final versions of the Malawi STED guide and the Dairy Sector report with ongoing technical assistance provided to support implementation of the strategy.</narrative>
   </description>
